    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d531">

                <pb facs="0641" n="631" sameAs="frus:frus1944v02/pg631"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">840.50/12–244</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The First Secretary of the British Embassy</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">White</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Director of the Office of Wartime Economic
                        Affairs</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Taft</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">Ref. 3498/2/44</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-12-02">2 December,
                        1944</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Taft</hi>: In Opie’s temporary absence, I am
                    sending you herewith a further memorandum in connection with the proposals for
                    the formation of a European Economic Committee.</p>
                <p>A similar communication is being addressed to the Soviet Government, but is not,
                    for the present, being made to other Allied Governments.</p>
                <p>We should be grateful for an early indication of the views of the United States
                    Government upon the proposal contained in the attached memorandum.</p>
                <p>Yours sincerely,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>E. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Wyndham White</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>


                <xi:include href="d531-a1.xml" xpointer="d531-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
